`audio-tools-avp/scripts/train_latch.py`. Either the box runs a newer checkout than anything
mirrored here, or that comment is stale.

Three different bugs hide behind that, with three different fixes:
  - linear resample  -> morph late and slowed (your diagnosis; fix = build the target at the
    padded length, or trim the generated grid before the head reads it)
  - truncate / pad at head -> morph on time, tail unguided (much milder)
  - `target_raw` not implemented -> **the chroma morph does nothing at all**, and has never
    done anything, in a2a_mix and anywhere else that passes a raw curve

